<hr>
<p>There are three steps to creating a new document with the Document API:<=
/p>
<ol class=3D"list">
<li>A request that provides metadata about the file to be uploaded.</li>
<li>One or more requests to upload the file in one or more parts.</li>
<li>A request that specifies the document metadata and references the uploa=
ded file(s) to complete the archival into OnBase.</li>
</ol>
<p>If the OnBase document will be comprised of multiple files, you need to =
repeat the first two steps in this process before executing the final reque=
st.</p>
<h2 id=3D"new-document-archive-scenarios">New Document Archive Scenarios</h=
2>
<p>There are 3 primary upload scenarios that exists:</p>
<ul class=3D"list">
<li>Single Part File Upload<ul class=3D"list">
<li>This scenario uploads the entire file in one request.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Multiple Part File Upload<ul class=3D"list">
<li>This scenario demonstrates the requests needed when a file must be brok=
en into parts because it is larger than the size you determined for a singl=
e upload request.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Multiple Files Upload<ul class=3D"list">
<li>In this scenario, the new document includes two files, so this example =
demonstrates how to stage and upload both files.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>For the examples below, there are some important notes:  </p>
<ol class=3D"list">
<li>These examples are assuming that the documents are stored into a non-re=
visable and non-renditionable document types.<ul class=3D"list">
<li>To upload a document as a new document irrespective of the document typ=
e settings, set <code>storeAsNew</code> property to <code>true</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Authorization and some other headers are excluded to simplify the examp=
les.</li>
<li>Likewise, for simplicity, the example Document Type has only Stand Alon=
e Keyword Types and no Single Instance or Multi-Instance Keyword Type Group=
s.</li>
<li>When uploading a new document, KeywordGuid can be obtained by making a =
request to <code>GET /document-types/{documentTypeId}/default-keywords</cod=
e></li>
<li>When uploading a revision or rendition to an existing document, Keyword=
Guid can be obtained by making a request to <code>GET /documents/{documentI=
d}/keywords</code></li>
<li>This is assuming that a Temp File Service already exists and is set up =
to talk to an S3 or a UNC storage.</li>
<li>The Document Management API deals with file sizes in bytes so all sizes=
 in requests and responses will be in bytes.</li>
</ol>
