vision</h2>
<p>When uploading a revision, the first two steps are still the same. We ne=
ed to set up the staging area by making a request to <code>POST /documents/=
uploads</code> and send in the bytes to <code>PUT /documents/uploads/{uploa=
dId}?filePart=3D#</code>.
The only difference is the last step which completes the upload process. In=
stead of doing a POST to <code>/documents/</code>, a POST to <code>/documen=
ts/{documentId}/revisions</code> should be made. This would add the documen=
t as the latest revision to the existing document.</p>
<h2 id=3D"uploading-a-new-rendition">Uploading a New Rendition</h2>
<p>Similar to revisions, the final request is made to <code>POST /documents=
/{documentId}/revisions/latest/renditions</code> instead.
Note that we always add rendition to <code>latest</code> revision.</p>
<h2 id=3D"uploading-a-new-document-to-a-revisable-or-renditionable-document=
-type">Uploading a New Document to a Revisable or Renditionable Document Ty=
pe</h2>
<p>When attempting to upload a new document to a Revisable/Renditionable do=
cument type, there might be a case where multiple documents are found match=
ing the given keywords. In that scenario, we return a <code>300 Multiple Ch=
oices</code> response with a list of document Ids that matches along with t=
he options available for that document. This example will use a 1 MB file (=
1048576 bytes).</p>
<p><strong>Request 1: Initiate upload</strong></p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">POST</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-string">/documents/uploads</span> HTTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: application/json

<span class=3D"json">{
  <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"fileExtension"</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-str=
ing">"jpg"</span>,
  <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"fileSize"</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">=
"1048576"</span>
}</span></code></pre><p><strong>Response 1: Created upload staging area</st=
rong></p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">201</span> C=
reated
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: application/json
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Location</span>: /documents/uploads/123

<span class=3D"json">{
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"id"</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">"123=
"</span>,
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"filePartSize"</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-nu=
mber">1048576</span>,
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"numberOfParts"</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-n=
umber">1</span>
}</span></code></pre><p><strong>Request 2: Upload all bytes</strong></p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PUT</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-string">/documents/uploads/123?filePart=3D1</span> HTTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Length</span>: 1048576

<span class=3D"maxima">&lt;binary-<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">part</span>=
-<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">content</span>&gt;</span></code></pre><p><st=
rong>Response 2: Received bytes</strong></p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">204</span> N=
o Content</code></pre><p><strong>Request 3: Archive document with upload an=
d metadata</strong></p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">POST</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-string">/documents</span> HTTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: application/json

<span class=3D"json">{
